at if we RESTRUCTURE so that find_profile returns the malformed/internal errors directly,\n# and resolve_value distinguishes missing from others by checking the error string?\n# \n# find_profile currently: fold over profiles; if p.id==key -> Ok(p); else keep acc (Err(nil) init, \n# becomes Err(E_H10_MISSING) after is-ok check). \n# We could change find_profile to, on match, return:\n#   if p.state == \\\"ok\\\" -> Ok(p)\n#   if p.state == \\\"malformed\\\" -> Err(\\\"E_H10_INVALID: <key>\\\")  [concat]\n#   if p.state == \\\"internal\\\" -> Err(\\\"E_H10_INTERNAL: <key>\\\")  [concat]\n# But that needs 2 err nodes + 1 ok node inside the fold — same problem.\n# \n# ALTERNATIVE: keep find_profile as-is (returns Ok(p) or Err(\\\"E_H10_MISSING\\\")), and change \n# resolve_value to:\n#   if is-ok(found): \n#       p = unwrap(found)\n#       if p.state == \\\"ok\\\": Ok(p.value)\n#       else: ??? need Err(E_H10_INVALID/INTERNAL: key)\n#   else: Ok(\\\"unknown\\\")   [missing]\n# The ??? still needs err nodes.\n# \n# What if resolve_value returns the error WITHOUT an err node by... no, result requires ok/err nodes.\n# \n# Hmm, wait. Let me reconsider: maybe the ok/err nodes ARE created by 'create_call' with \n# name='ok'/'err' AND the dispatcher stores them as ok/err nodes, but my inspection shows \n# 'call' because... no, inspect clearly shows kind=call.\n# \n# Let me check whether there's a create tool for OTHER result-ish nodes like 'create_err' in \n# the dispatcher by testing the exact tool name 'create_err' with various params — we did; unknown.\n# \n# Let me look at the dispatcher implementation ONE more time. The strings showed:\n# \\\"create_literal: unsupported type \\\" (create_literal)\n# \\\"E_AEP_001: unknown node kind\\\" (create_node)\n# \\\"E_AEP_002: node kind '...' does not allow field '...'\\\" (set_field)\n# \\\"E_AEP_003: node kind '...' does not allow slot '...'\\\" (replace_slot)\n# \\\"E_AEP_004/005/006/007: node kind ...\\\" (append_child etc.)\